```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: Password Spray Against Multiple Accounts
# Detection ID: DE-CA-003
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1110.003 - Brute Force: Password Spraying
# Data Source: Windows Security 4625 / Azure AD Sign-In Logs
# Severity: High
# ============================================================================

index=auth (sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4625) OR sourcetype="azure:aad:signin"
| eval src_ip=coalesce(src_ip, IpAddress), account=coalesce(TargetUserName, UserPrincipalName)
| bucket _time span=10m
| stats dc(account) as unique_accounts_targeted count as total_failures values(account) as accounts by src_ip, _time
| where unique_accounts_targeted>=8 AND total_failures>=10
| sort -unique_accounts_targeted
```

## Detection Logic
Password spraying is characterized by a single source hitting many distinct accounts with low per-account attempt counts, evading traditional lockout-threshold brute-force detections. This search buckets failures into 10-minute windows and flags sources with high account fan-out.

## False Positive Considerations
Shared NAT egress (corporate VPN exit nodes, cloud egress IPs) can create false fan-out — correlate src_ip against known corporate egress ranges lookup before alerting.

## Tuning Notes
Tune unique_accounts_targeted and total_failures thresholds based on your tenant size; 8/10m works for mid-size (500-5000 user) environments.
